{"model":"qwen2.5-coder:32b","created_at":"2026-08-10T18:35:32.465933Z","response":"# Design Specification for Reimplementation of `util.h` and `util.cpp`\n\n## Overview\n\nThis document provides a detailed design specification for the reimplementation of two C++ source files: `util.h` (header file) and `util.cpp` (source file). The primary goal is to ensure that the new implementation adheres strictly to the original structure, namespaces, types, signatures, and identifiers as specified in the provided code.\n\n## Target-Owned Inputs\n\n- **Identifiers**: Fxx/Uxx identifiers are opaque. Preserve names, types, signatures, namespaces, and replacement boundaries.\n- **Replacement Units**:\n  - `F01/U01`: `include/util.h`\n  - `F02/U02`: `src/util/util.cpp`\n\n## File: `util.h`\n\n### Path\n`include/util.h`\n\n### Role\nComplete target-owned implementation/declaration file.\n\n### Replacement Required\nTrue\n\n### File Description\nThis header file contains common utility functions and classes used throughout the project. It includes functionalities for string manipulation, YAML parsing, file descriptor management, thread operations, backtrace generation, and RAII patterns.\n\n### Dependencies\n- `fmt/format.h`\n- `yaml-cpp/yaml.h`\n- `\u003csys/stat.h\u003e`\n- `\u003cconcepts\u003e`\n- `\u003cfunctional\u003e`\n- `\u003cinitializer_list\u003e`\n- `\u003cmemory\u003e`\n- `\u003cregex\u003e`\n- `\u003cstring\u003e`\n- `\u003cstring_view\u003e`\n- `\u003cutility\u003e`\n- `\u003cvector\u003e`\n\n### Namespace\n`ws`\n\n### Constants and Types\n\n1. **FileDescriptor**\n   - Type: `int`\n   - Description: The underlying type of file descriptors.\n\n2. **invalid_file_descriptor**\n   - Type: `constexpr FileDescriptor`\n   - Value: `-1`\n   - Description: A constant value representing invalid file descriptors.\n\n### Functions\n\n1. **StringToLower**\n   - Signature: `std::string StringToLower(std::string str) noexcept;`\n   - Description: Converts a string into lower-case.\n\n2. **StringToUpper**\n   - Signature: `std::string StringToUpper(std::string str) noexcept;`\n   - Description: Converts a string into upper-case.\n\n3. **ReplaceAllSubstring**\n   - Signature: `std::string ReplaceAllSubstring(std::string_view str, std::string_view from, std::string_view to) noexcept;`\n   - Description: Replaces all occurrences of a sub-string in a string.\n\n4. **SplitString**\n   - Signature: `std::vector\u003cstd::string\u003e SplitString(const std::string\u0026 str, const std::regex\u0026 pattern) noexcept;`\n   - Description: Splits a string by a regex pattern.\n\n5. **SplitStringToLines**\n   - Signature: `std::vector\u003cstd::string\u003e SplitStringToLines(const std::string\u0026 str) noexcept;`\n   - Description: Splits a string into lines.\n\n6. **LoadYamlString**\n   - Signature: `YAML::Node LoadYamlString(std::string_view str, std::initializer_list\u003cstd::string_view\u003e required_fields = {});`\n   - Description: Loads a YAML node from a string.\n   - Exceptions:\n     - Throws `std::invalid_argument` if the node does not contain all required fields.\n\n7. **ThrowIfYamlFieldIsNotScalar**\n   - Signature: `void ThrowIfYamlFieldIsNotScalar(const YAML::Node\u0026 node, std::string_view field);`\n   - Description: Throws an `std::invalid_argument` exception if a field does not exist in a YAML node or it is not scalar.\n\n8. **IsValidFileDescriptor**\n   - Signature: `constexpr bool IsValidFileDescriptor(FileDescriptor fd) noexcept;`\n   - Description: Checks whether a file descriptor is valid.\n   - Note: Assumes the value of valid file descriptors should be greater than or equal to 0.\n\n9. **SetFileDescriptorAsNonblocking**\n   - Signature: `void SetFileDescriptorAsNonblocking(FileDescriptor fd);`\n   - Description: Sets a file descriptor as non-blocking.\n   - Exceptions:\n     - Throws `std::system_error` if setting the file descriptor fails.\n\n10. **ThrowLastSystemError**\n    - Signature: `[[noreturn]] void ThrowLastSystemError();`\n    - Description: Throws a `std::system_error` exception containing the last-error.\n\n11. **CurrentThreadId**\n    - Signature: `std::uint32_t CurrentThreadId() noexcept;`\n    - Description: Gets the ID of the current thread.\n\n12. **Backtrace (Overloaded)**\n    - Signature 1: `void Backtrace(std::vector\u003cstd::string\u003e\u0026 stack, std::size_t size, std::size_t skip = 0) noexcept;`\n      - Description: Gets a backtrace for the calling program.\n    - Signature 2: `std::string Backtrace(std::size_t size, std::size_t skip = 0, std::string_view prefix = \"\") noexcept;`\n      - Description: Gets a backtrace for the calling program and returns it as a string.\n\n### Classes\n\n1. **Singleton**\n   - Template Parameters:\n     - `T`: A type using the singleton pattern.\n     - `Args`: The arguments of the singleton instance, referring to one of its constructors.\n   - Methods:\n     - `Instance()`: Gets the singleton instance.\n\n2. **SingletonPtr**\n   - Template Parameters:\n     - `T`: A type using the singleton pattern.\n     - `Args`: The argument types of the singleton instance, referring to one of its constructors.\n   - Methods:\n     - `Instance()`: Gets the singleton instance.\n\n3. **RAII**\n   - Template Parameters:\n     - `T`: An object needing to be cleaned.\n     - `Cleaner`: A cleaner function type.\n   - Requirements:\n     - `std::is_invocable_v\u003cCleaner, T\u003e`\n   - Methods:\n     - Constructor: Creates an RAII for an object.\n     - Deleted Copy and Move Operations\n     - Destructor: Cleans the object using the provided cleaner.\n\n4. **MappedReadOnlyFile**\n   - Description: RAII for a read-only file that has been mapped into memory.\n   - Methods:\n     - Default Constructor\n     - Deleted Copy Operations\n     - Move Constructor and Assignment Operator\n     - Destructor: Unmaps the file.\n     - `Map(std::string path)`: Maps a file into memory.\n       - Exceptions:\n         - Throws `std::invalid_argument` if the path refers to a directory.\n         - Throws `std::runtime_error` if no permission to access the file.\n         - Throws `std::system_error` if mapping the file fails.\n     - `Unmap()`: Unmaps the file.\n     - `Size()`: Gets the file size.\n     - `Data()`: Gets the file data.\n     - `Path()`: Gets the file path.\n\n### Concepts\n\n1. **Addable**\n   - Template Parameters:\n     - `T`\n     - `U`\n     - `Ret = T`\n   - Requirements:\n     - `{ t + u } -\u003e std::convertible_to\u003cRet\u003e`\n\n## File: `util.cpp`\n\n### Path\n`src/util/util.cpp`\n\n### Role\nComplete target-owned implementation/declaration file.\n\n### Replacement Required\nTrue\n\n### File Description\nThis source file contains the implementations of the utility functions and classes declared in `util.h`.\n\n### Dependencies\n- `\"util.h\"`\n- `\u003cexecinfo.h\u003e`\n- `\u003cfcntl.h\u003e`\n- `\u003csys/mman.h\u003e`\n- `\u003csys/syscall.h\u003e`\n- `\u003cunistd.h\u003e`\n- `\u003calgorithm\u003e`\n- `\u003ccassert\u003e`\n- `\u003ccerrno\u003e`\n- `\u003citerator\u003e`\n- `\u003csstream\u003e`\n- `\u003csystem_error\u003e`\n\n### Namespace\n`ws`\n\n### Function Implementations\n\n1. **StringToLower**\n   - Implementation: Uses `std::ranges::transform` to convert each character in the string to lower-case.\n\n2. **StringToUpper**\n   - Implementation: Uses `std::ranges::transform` to convert each character in the string to upper-case.\n\n3. **ReplaceAllSubstring**\n   - Implementation: Iterates through the string, replacing all occurrences of a sub-string with another sub-string using an output stream.\n\n4. **SplitString**\n   - Implementation: Utilizes `std::sregex_token_iterator` to split the string based on a regex pattern and stores the results in a vector.\n\n5. **SplitStringToLines**\n   - Implementation: Uses a predefined regex pattern for newline characters to split the string into lines.\n\n6. **LoadYamlString**\n   - Implementation: Loads a YAML node from a string using `YAML::Load` and checks if all required fields are present.\n   - Exceptions:\n     - Throws `std::invalid_argument` if any required field is missing.\n\n7. **ThrowIfYamlFieldIsNotScalar**\n   - Implementation: Checks if the specified field exists in the YAML node and whether it is a scalar.\n   - Exceptions:\n     - Throws `std::invalid_argument` if the field does not exist or is not a scalar.\n\n8. **ThrowLastSystemError**\n   - Implementation: Throws a `std::system_error` exception containing the last system error code.\n\n9. **SetFileDescriptorAsNonblocking**\n   - Implementation: Uses `fcntl` to set the file descriptor as non-blocking.\n   - Exceptions:\n     - Throws `std::system_error` if setting the file descriptor fails.\n\n10. **CurrentThreadId**\n    - Implementation: Retrieves the current thread ID using `syscall(SYS_gettid)`.\n\n11. **Backtrace (Overloaded)**\n    - Implementation 1: Uses `backtrace` and `backtrace_symbols` to generate a backtrace and stores it in a vector.\n    - Implementation 2: Calls the first implementation of `Backtrace` and formats the result into a string with an optional prefix.\n\n### Class Implementations\n\n1. **MappedReadOnlyFile**\n   - Methods:\n     - Default Constructor\n     - Move Constructor and Assignment Operator\n     - Destructor: Unmaps the file.\n     - `Map(std::string path)`: Maps a file into memory using `mmap`.\n       - Exceptions:\n         - Throws `std::invalid_argument` if the path refers to a directory.\n         - Throws `std::runtime_error` if no permission to access the file.\n         - Throws `std::system_error` if mapping the file fails.\n     - `Unmap()`: Unmaps the file using `munmap`.\n     - `Size()`: Returns the size of the mapped file.\n     - `Data()`: Returns a pointer to the mapped data.\n     - `Path()`: Returns the path of the mapped file.\n\n2. **Check**\n   - Private Method: Validates the file before mapping it into memory.\n   - Exceptions:\n     - Throws `std::invalid_argument` if the path refers to a directory.\n     - Throws `std::runtime_error` if no permission to access the file.\n     - Throws `std::system_error` for other system errors.\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThis design specification provides a comprehensive guide for reimplementing the utility functions and classes in `util.h` and `util.cpp`. The new implementation should strictly adhere to the original structure, namespaces, types, signatures, and identifiers as specified.","done":true,"done_reason":"stop","context":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,57218,57842,129542,34,1027,124867,60298,140653,29412,106637,14682,5373,50230,124867,60298,140653,29412,109037,129692,136546,4086,44,28195,87256,127231,98641,126241,124808,5373,117625,25770,106528,107669,127123,102171,127917,12857,134093,3407,17254,47534,53931,114277,129692,134481,15322,83751,107636,129306,16161,71215,3407,45583,12,7583,1479,26149,50,198,37,4146,62010,4146,47216,525,46484,13,81306,5036,11,4494,11,32628,11,58091,11,323,13723,22711,304,279,1590,25128,382,787,2916,88806,38202,17126,198,7308,13723,18743,11265,8153,686,387,70353,13,17207,15382,8153,1969,6051,279,2884,714,1969,537,3635,2550,8153,624,787,2916,88806,6643,14474,25,434,15,16,62010,15,16,11,434,15,17,62010,15,17,198,81076,12,31092,26149,50,25,6857,271,46725,22203,434,15,16,62010,15,16,30742,198,2343,25,2924,22610,860,198,5778,25,4583,2169,28699,8129,14,80383,1034,198,83631,18743,25,830,198,1747,353,569,1192,4094,860,198,353,569,6658,7718,398,1483,29419,624,1213,353,569,3094,24495,33349,724,16739,78,320,7522,40950,16,15,23,31,411,7201,905,340,353,569,1732,32095,198,353,3703,1110,5204,905,71960,16739,8535,15998,198,353,569,4366,220,16,13,15,198,353,569,1028,220,17,15,17,17,12,15,19,12,17,18,198,1213,353,569,8687,7032,22610,4452,7208,198,1213,353,569,17370,29558,569,79,8879,448,356,1027,17,15,569,79,3561,624,2791,6490,3055,271,1067,366,12501,92340,860,397,1067,366,41466,1786,602,26491,94